WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:17.295
BEN: Hello, Little Fox readers, and welcome to the latest edition of People in the News . Do

2
00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:23.532
any of you like to play soccer? Well, guess what . . . Today's person in the news is

3
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:34.439
one of the greatest soccer players in the world. OLIVIA: That's right, Ben. I'm going to introduce you

4
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.439
to Lionel Messi, who plays professional soccer (also called football in some parts of the world) for two

5
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.524
different teams: the FC Barcelona club in Spain and the national team of Argentina. During his career Leo has

6
00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:51.831
become known as one of the best soccer players of all time. That's a huge feat for one

7
00:00:51.832 --> 00:01:03.511
of the smallest players on the field today! Leo was born in Rosario, Argentina, on June 24, 1987.

8
00:01:03.512 --> 00:01:11.074
His father was a steelworker and his mother worked part-time as a cleaner. Leo started playing soccer when he

9
00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:18.400
was just five years old, often using a soda can or stone as a ball. According to a

10
00:01:18.401 --> 00:01:24.661
family story, the first time he played, nothing happened when the ball came to his right foot. But

11
00:01:24.662 --> 00:01:33.319
when the ball rolled toward his left foot, he started dribbling as if he'd been playing forever! Soon Leo

12
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:42.878
joined a local soccer club, where people noticed his dribbling skills, along with his incredible speed and agility.

13
00:01:42.879 --> 00:01:51.219
By the time Leo was 11, many people had noticed something else about him: Leo was a lot

14
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:57.695
smaller than most of the other boys on the field. Eventually doctors realized that Leo had a growth hormone

15
00:01:57.696 --> 00:02:04.861
deficiency, a disorder that leads to slow growth in children. The medication for the disorder was very expensive,

16
00:02:04.862 --> 00:02:11.606
and his family needed help with paying for it. So when one of the best soccer teams in

17
00:02:11.607 --> 00:02:16.262
the world, FC Barcelona, expressed interest in Leo—and offered to pay his medical bills—he left Argentina and moved with

18
00:02:16.263 --> 00:02:22.261
his father to Spain. Leo was 13 when he joined the Barcelona team's youth academy. He was quite

19
00:02:22.262 --> 00:02:31.095
thin and short, standing only around 138 centimeters tall. His small size made him shy and quiet, so

20
00:02:31.096 --> 00:02:44.165
quiet in fact that he barely said a word for his first month with the team. But when the

21
00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:50.234
coaches warned other players not to tackle little Leo too aggressively because he'd get hurt, the players just

22
00:02:50.235 --> 00:02:55.510
laughed and said they couldn't tackle Leo—he was too fast to catch! Leo trained at the academy for

23
00:02:55.511 --> 00:03:05.147
several years, moving up quickly through the junior ranks. When he was 16, he played in the top division

24
00:03:05.148 --> 00:03:12.655
for the first time. The following year he broke a team record when he became the youngest player—age

25
00:03:12.656 --> 00:03:15.318
17—to score a goal for Barcelona during a league game. From that point on, Leo, with his powerful

26
00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:24.216
left foot, was a sensation in the world of professional soccer. BEN: Did the medication help Leo? OLIVIA: Yes,

27
00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:31.390
although he's still pretty small for a professional male athlete, about 169 centimeters tall. In 2004 Leo was

28
00:03:31.391 --> 00:03:37.888
offered a chance to play international soccer on Spain's national team. But he declined, saying that he wanted

29
00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:49.948
to play for Argentina, the country where he had been born. Since then Leo has participated in many major

30
00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:56.042
events for Argentina, including the World Cup—that's the competition held every four years for the world's best soccer

31
00:03:56.043 --> 00:04:03.431
teams. What makes Leo such a fantastic player is his amazing speed and skill with the ball. In

32
00:04:03.432 --> 00:04:10.938
fact, because of his small size and ability to dart up and down the field, his nickname is the

33
00:04:10.939 --> 00:04:19.417
"Flea." Some people say that Leo "feels" the ball and can change direction faster than any other player

34
00:04:19.418 --> 00:04:23.421
can. He also just loves to play. He's told reporters that he has lots of fun playing soccer,

35
00:04:23.422 --> 00:04:27.656
just like a boy playing on the street! BEN: So is Leo the greatest soccer player ever? OLIVIA: Well,

36
00:04:27.657 --> 00:04:34.066
Ben, soccer fans love to argue about that. Some fans claim that Leo can't be called the best

37
00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:42.822
until he helps Argentina win a World Cup title. And many Argentine fans question Leo's loyalty since his

38
00:04:42.823 --> 00:04:53.651
record with Argentina is weaker than his record with his Spanish team. But Leo strongly defends his pride in

39
00:04:53.652 --> 00:04:59.141
playing for Argentina, insisting that he has never stopped being Argentine even though he lives in Spain now.

40
00:04:59.142 --> 00:05:08.062
One thing is certain: Leo has earned a lot of money playing soccer. He is among the highest

41
00:05:08.063 --> 00:05:17.374
paid athletes in the world, earning millions of dollars a year for playing soccer and endorsing dozens of products.

42
00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:21.291
Off the field Leo is still a quiet, reserved person who tries to follow the values he learned

43
00:05:21.292 --> 00:05:30.627
as a kid—being humble and showing respect to others. And he's also quite busy with many causes that

44
00:05:30.628 --> 00:05:36.276
help kids. Because of his own childhood health problems, he established the Leo Messi Foundation to provide access to

45
00:05:36.277 --> 00:05:43.355
education and health care for kids at risk. In another volunteer position, he serves as a goodwill ambassador

46
00:05:43.356 --> 00:05:48.353
for the United Nations, traveling around the world to spotlight issues that affect children such as poverty and

47
00:05:48.354 --> 00:05:53.778
homelessness. Meanwhile Leo is still scoring plenty of goals on the soccer field. In 2014 he became Barcelona's all-time

48
00:05:53.779 --> 00:06:02.002
top scorer. And he's won all of the sport's biggest trophies, including being named the World Player of

49
00:06:02.003 --> 00:06:05.753
the Year four times! BEN: Wow, thanks for telling us about Lionel Messi, Olivia. The "Flea" might be

50
00:06:05.754 --> 00:06:13.419
one of the smallest players on the field today, but he's certainly a giant among professional soccer players! And

51
00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:21.206
thanks to you, Little Fox readers, for tuning in to another edition of People in the News !

